    "story": {
      "type": "about-story",
      "blocks": {
        "header": {
          "type": "group",
          "settings": {
            "direction": "column",
            "gap": "md"
          },
          "blocks": {
            "eyebrow": {
              "type": "text",
              "settings": {
                "text": "<p>Our story</p>",
                "style": "eyebrow"
              }
            },
            "heading": {
              "type": "heading",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "It started in other people's clubs",
                "tag": "h2",
                "size": "lg"
              }
            }
          },
          "block_order": [
            "eyebrow",
            "heading"
          ],
          "static": true
        },
        "paragraph-1": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Before Fencing Club, we spent years visiting fencing clubs, schools, and training halls around the world. Everywhere we went, we saw the same problem. The gear fencers needed was hard to find, quality changed from one batch to the next, and long, indirect supply chains pushed prices up.</p>",
            "style": "lead"
          }
        },
        "paragraph-2": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>It didn't matter whether someone was picking up a foil for the first time or training for the finals. Getting reliable equipment was slow, expensive, or a gamble.</p>",
            "style": "lead"
          }
        },
        "belief": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Cost and access should never stand between a fencer and the sport.</p>",
            "style": "lead"
          }
        },
        "paragraph-3": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>So in 2023 we opened Fencing Club in Woodinville, near Seattle: one shop for fencing gear and nothing else, buying direct from the makers and answering every question ourselves. We sold our first 1,000 orders offline, before the web store even opened.</p>",
            "style": "lead"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "paragraph-1",
        "paragraph-2",
        "belief",
        "paragraph-3"
      ]
    },
    "clubs": {
      "type": "about-clubs",
      "blocks": {
        "header": {
          "type": "group",
          "settings": {
            "direction": "column",
            "gap": "md"
          },
          "blocks": {
            "eyebrow": {
              "type": "text",
              "settings": {
                "text": "<p>USA Fencing Region 1</p>",
                "style": "eyebrow"
              }
            },
            "heading": {
              "type": "heading",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "The clubs we call home",
                "tag": "h2",
                "size": "lg"
              }
            },
            "intro": {
              "type": "text",
              "settings": {
                "text": "<p>You'll find our team on the piste most weeks, fencing épée at Kaizen Academy and Olympic Epee Masters, foil at Rain City Fencing Center, and open fencing at Salle Auriol. If you train at one of them, come say hello.</p>",
                "style": "lead"
              }
            }
          },
          "block_order": [
            "eyebrow",
            "heading",
            "intro"
          ],
          "static": true
        },
